IMPORT prelude

-- Sale of Commercial Properties Act 1979 (Singapore) -- when the Act applies to a sale of a commercial unit (s 11(1)), what counts as
-- a sale (s 3(2), (3)), the ban on selling before building plans are approved (s 3(1)), the prescribed option and agreement forms
-- (ss 4, 5), the developer's duty not to take anonymous money (s 5A(1)), who may not be a substantial shareholder of a developer or
-- hold a responsible position in one (ss 5D, 5E), the Controller's directions to a defaulting developer and the purchaser's
-- liquidated damages (s 8), officers' liability (s 9), composition (s 9A), and the maximum penalties (ss 5A to 5E, 6, 7, 7A, 8, 10(3)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to 1 December 2021, in operation 31 December 2021), informal
-- consolidation "version in force from 1/7/2025", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SCPA1979.txt. The latest amendment
-- annotated is Act 15 of 2025 with effect from 1 July 2025 (the Anti-Money Laundering and Other Matters (Estate Agents and Developers)
-- Act 2025, as s 5D(1)(a) names it); Act 54 of 2018 is annotated in force from 28 June 2023. THE ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS AT THE TOP
-- OF THE DEPOSIT IS ONE LINE OUT OF STEP WITH THE BODY (it pairs "2." with "Short title"); this encoding follows the section numbers
-- in the body.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0031 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet. The
-- Act is short, so nearly all of its operative provisions are taken. Not encoded: the definitions beyond what the rules below need;
-- the content of the customer due diligence, record-keeping and programme duties in ss 5A(2) to (4), 5B and 5C (only their penalty);
-- the Controller's production powers in s 7A beyond the s 7A(4) penalty; the rule-making power in s 10 beyond the s 10(3) cap; s 12
-- (court jurisdiction). The prescribed option form, agreement terms, deposit limits, instalment schedule and compoundable offences
-- live in rules made under s 10, which were NOT retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the finished naive rows (the writing-l4-rules
-- skill was not available in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Sale of Commercial Properties Act 1979 -- sales`

§§ `11(1) -- when the Act applies`

-- s 11(1): "This Act does not apply to the sale of any commercial property -- (a) in a building containing, or a building which when
-- erected will contain, not more than 4 separate units; or (b) where the certificate of statutory completion has been issued by the
-- Building Authority and the subsidiary strata certificate of title, if applicable, has been issued by the Registrar of Titles".
-- s 11(2): the Minister may by Gazette notification exempt any person or commercial property "from any of the provisions"; this
-- encoding treats an exemption as total (a simplification: a real exemption may cover only some provisions or carry conditions).
GIVEN `the units are statutorily completed` IS A BOOLEAN, `strata title applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `strata title is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the completion exemption applies` IF
    `the units are statutorily completed` AND ((NOT `strata title applies`) OR `strata title is issued`)

GIVEN `separate units in the building` IS A NUMBER,
      `certificate of statutory completion issued` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a strata title is applicable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the strata title has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `exempted by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to the sale` IF
        `separate units in the building` GREATER THAN 4
    AND (NOT (`the completion exemption applies` `certificate of statutory completion issued` `a strata title is applicable` `the strata title has been issued`))
    AND (NOT `exempted by the Minister`)

§§ `3(2), (3) -- what is a sale`

-- s 3(2): a person sells a commercial property if "(a) by an agreement in writing, the person agrees to divest the person's estate or
-- interest in the commercial property to another person for valuable consideration; or (b) by any deed or instrument, the person
-- conveys, assigns, demises or otherwise disposes of the commercial property" so that it becomes registrable.
-- s 3(3): "A lease or an agreement for a lease for a term of years not exceeding 7 years without the option of renewal or purchase is
-- not to be deemed a sale".
GIVEN `it is a lease` IS A BOOLEAN, `term in years` IS A NUMBER, `with an option of renewal or purchase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the short-lease carve-out applies` IF
    `it is a lease` AND `term in years` AT MOST 7 AND (NOT `with an option of renewal or purchase`)

GIVEN `a written agreement to divest for value` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a registrable disposition by deed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the transaction is a lease` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the lease term in years` IS A NUMBER,
      `the lease has an option of renewal or purchase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transaction is a sale` IF
        (`a written agreement to divest for value` OR `a registrable disposition by deed`)
    AND (NOT (`the short-lease carve-out applies` `the transaction is a lease` `the lease term in years` `the lease has an option of renewal or purchase`))

§§ `3(1) and 6 -- no sale before the building plans are approved`

-- s 3(1): "A person must not sell any commercial property unless the plans for the construction or erection of the commercial
-- property have been approved by the Building Authority." The duty is on "a person", not only a developer.
-- s 6: "Any person who fails to comply with any of the provisions of this Act shall be guilty of an offence" -- $10,000 or one year
-- or both. (s 3 carries no penalty of its own; that s 6 is its penalty is an inference from s 6's words "any of the provisions".)
GIVEN `the Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is a sale` IS A BOOLEAN, `the building plans are approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sale breaches s 3` IF
    `the Act applies` AND `it is a sale` AND (NOT `the building plans are approved`)

§§ `4, 5 -- the option and the agreement`

-- s 4: an option to purchase "must be in such form as may be prescribed, except that any additional term or condition which in
-- substance does not affect the prescribed form may be included".
-- s 5(2): a term of the sale and purchase agreement "which is inconsistent with the terms and conditions of sale prescribed ... is to
-- the extent of the inconsistency void".
GIVEN `in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN, `has an additional term` IS A BOOLEAN, `the additional term affects the prescribed form in substance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the option complies with s 4` IF
    `in the prescribed form` AND ((NOT `has an additional term`) OR (NOT `the additional term affects the prescribed form in substance`))

-- (s 5(2) is a one-line identity -- an inconsistent term is void to the extent of the inconsistency -- and is left as this comment;
-- what is inconsistent depends on the prescribed terms, which were not retrieved.)

§§ `5A(1) -- no anonymous money`

-- s 5A(1): a developer must not "open or maintain any account for, or hold and receive moneys from -- (a) an anonymous source; or (b) a
-- purchaser with an obviously fictitious name". Penalty (s 5A(5)): fine not exceeding $100,000.
GIVEN `the source is anonymous` IS A BOOLEAN, `the purchaser's name is obviously fictitious` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the developer may receive the moneys` IF
    (NOT `the source is anonymous`) AND (NOT `the purchaser's name is obviously fictitious`)

§§ `5E -- who may not hold a responsible position in a developer`

-- s 5E(3): "responsible position" means (a) for a company "a director, manager or secretary"; (b) for a society "a president,
-- secretary or treasurer"; (c) for a partnership "a partner"; (d) for a limited liability partnership "a partner or manager"; (e) for
-- a group of persons "any person in that group". (The "position analogous to" limbs are not modelled.)
DECLARE DeveloperForm IS ONE OF
    `a company`
    `a society`
    `a partnership`
    `a limited liability partnership`
    `a group of persons`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `director`
    `manager`
    `secretary`
    `president`
    `treasurer`
    `partner`
    `member of the group`
    `shareholder only`
    `ordinary employee`

GIVEN `the form` IS A DeveloperForm, `the role` IS A Role
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the role is a responsible position` IF
    CONSIDER `the form`
    WHEN `a company` THEN `the role` EQUALS `director` OR `the role` EQUALS `manager` OR `the role` EQUALS `secretary`
    WHEN `a society` THEN `the role` EQUALS `president` OR `the role` EQUALS `secretary` OR `the role` EQUALS `treasurer`
    WHEN `a partnership` THEN `the role` EQUALS `partner`
    WHEN `a limited liability partnership` THEN `the role` EQUALS `partner` OR `the role` EQUALS `manager`
    WHEN `a group of persons` THEN `the role` EQUALS `member of the group`

-- s 5E(1): must not hold a responsible position: (a) a person convicted of a money laundering, proliferation financing or terrorism
-- financing offence; (b) a person convicted "of an offence (whether in Singapore or elsewhere ...) involving fraud or dishonesty";
-- (c) "an undischarged bankrupt (whether in Singapore or elsewhere) or who suspends payment to or compounds with the person's
-- creditors".
-- s 5E(2): the (b) disqualification "ceases for a person at the end of 5 years beginning from -- (a) the date of the person's
-- conviction; or (b) if the person is imprisoned, the date on which the person convicted is released from custody, whichever date is
-- later". The (a) and (c) disqualifications have no time limit in the text.
-- Dates are modelled as whole years; "the end of 5 years" is taken as reached in the fifth year after the later date (an
-- approximation: the text runs from a date, not a year).
GIVEN `conviction year` IS A NUMBER, `imprisoned` IS A BOOLEAN, `release year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year the 5 years run from` MEANS
    IF `imprisoned` AND `release year` GREATER THAN `conviction year` THEN `release year` ELSE `conviction year`

GIVEN `convicted of a money laundering offence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `convicted of fraud or dishonesty` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `year convicted` IS A NUMBER,
      `was imprisoned` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `year released` IS A NUMBER,
      `undischarged bankrupt or compounded with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the year now` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `disqualified from a responsible position` IF
        `convicted of a money laundering offence`
    OR  (`convicted of fraud or dishonesty` AND `the year now` LESS THAN `the year the 5 years run from` `year convicted` `was imprisoned` `year released` PLUS 5)
    OR  `undischarged bankrupt or compounded with creditors`

§§ `5D -- who may not be a substantial shareholder of a developer`

-- s 5D(1): must not be or become a substantial shareholder of a developer: (a) a person convicted of a money laundering,
-- proliferation financing or terrorism financing offence; or (b) a company, partnership, society or LLP "which has an individual
-- mentioned in paragraph (a) holding a responsible position" in it. Fraud, dishonesty and bankruptcy are NOT grounds here.
GIVEN `convicted of a money laundering offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `an entity with such a convict in a responsible position` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `barred from being a substantial shareholder` IF
    `convicted of a money laundering offence` OR `an entity with such a convict in a responsible position`

§§ `8 -- the Controller's directions and liquidated damages`

-- s 8(1): where a developer "has sold any commercial property" and has not done any of (a) to (f) -- sought or complied with the
-- Registrar's direction under s 16 Land Titles Act; applied for subdivision permission; employed a registered surveyor; obtained the
-- subsidiary strata certificate of title; discharged a mortgage so as to complete; "executed and delivered to the purchaser an
-- assurance ... on or before the date fixed for completion" -- the Controller "may, in his or her discretion, issue directions".
-- s 8(5): the powers extend to property sold "at any time before 20 July 1979".
-- s 8(3): exercising the power "does not prejudice the right of the purchaser to claim liquidated damages for the developer's failure
-- to complete ... on or before the date appointed".
GIVEN `the developer has sold a commercial property` IS A BOOLEAN, `a default in s 8(1)(a) to (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Controller may direct the developer` IF
    `the developer has sold a commercial property` AND `a default in s 8(1)(a) to (f)`

GIVEN `the developer failed to complete by the agreed date` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Controller has given directions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purchaser may claim liquidated damages` IF
    `the developer failed to complete by the agreed date`

§§ `9 -- officers of a body corporate`

-- s 9: where a body corporate is guilty, any director, manager, secretary or similar officer (or person purporting to act as one)
-- "shall be guilty of the offence ... unless the person proves that the offence was committed without his or her consent or
-- connivance AND that he or she exercised all such diligence to prevent the commission of the offence as he or she ought". Both
-- limbs must be proved.
GIVEN `the body corporate is guilty` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `was an officer at the time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proves no consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proves due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is guilty too` IF
        `the body corporate is guilty` AND `was an officer at the time`
    AND (NOT (`proves no consent or connivance` AND `proves due diligence`))

§§ `Penalties -- ss 5A to 5E, 6, 7, 7A, 8, 10(3)`

-- s 5A(5), 5B(5), 5C(6), 5D(2), 5E(4), 7A(4): "a fine not exceeding $100,000" (no imprisonment).
-- s 5E(5) (contravening s 5E(1)(b) or (c)): "a fine not exceeding $50,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to
-- both".
-- s 6 (any provision without its own penalty, inferred to include s 3): "$10,000 or ... imprisonment ... not exceeding one year".
-- s 7(2) (a direction to ensure compliance): "$10,000 and to a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day during which the offence
-- continues after conviction" (no imprisonment).
-- s 8(2) (a s 8(1) direction): "$10,000 or ... imprisonment ... not exceeding one year or to both and to a further fine not exceeding
-- $1,000 for every day".
-- s 10(3)(b): penalties in rules "shall not exceed imprisonment for a term of 6 months or a fine of $10,000 or both".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `selling before plans are approved`
    `taking anonymous money`
    `failing to keep due diligence records`
    `having no anti-money laundering programme`
    `a disqualified substantial shareholder`
    `holding a responsible position after a money laundering conviction`
    `holding a responsible position after fraud or while bankrupt`
    `disobeying a compliance direction`
    `false information to the Controller`
    `disobeying a section 8 direction`
    `breaching the rules at the rules' maximum`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `selling before plans are approved` THEN 10000
    WHEN `taking anonymous money` THEN 100000
    WHEN `failing to keep due diligence records` THEN 100000
    WHEN `having no anti-money laundering programme` THEN 100000
    WHEN `a disqualified substantial shareholder` THEN 100000
    WHEN `holding a responsible position after a money laundering conviction` THEN 100000
    WHEN `holding a responsible position after fraud or while bankrupt` THEN 50000
    WHEN `disobeying a compliance direction` THEN 10000
    WHEN `false information to the Controller` THEN 100000
    WHEN `disobeying a section 8 direction` THEN 10000
    WHEN `breaching the rules at the rules' maximum` THEN 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `selling before plans are approved` THEN 12
    WHEN `holding a responsible position after fraud or while bankrupt` THEN 36
    WHEN `disobeying a section 8 direction` THEN 12
    WHEN `breaching the rules at the rules' maximum` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the further daily fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `disobeying a compliance direction` THEN 1000
    WHEN `disobeying a section 8 direction` THEN 1000
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum total fine` MEANS
    `the maximum fine` `the offence` PLUS `the further daily fine` `the offence` TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

-- s 9A(1): the Controller may compound an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence by collecting ... a sum not exceeding one half
-- of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence". (Which offences are compoundable is prescribed by rules not
-- retrieved; this gives the ceiling only.) s 9A(2): on payment "no further proceedings may be taken".
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    `the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2
